# Project Memory (local, via MCP)

This project has a local memory tool available: `remember`, `recall`, `list_memories`.
Use `project_id` = the repo folder name (e.g. "micromem").

## When to call `remember`
- We make an architectural or library decision (and why).
- We hit a non-obvious gotcha or bug and its fix.
- We set a convention (naming, folder structure, tooling choice).
- The user states a lasting preference about how this project should be built.

Do NOT log routine implementation details, ephemeral debugging, or anything
already obvious from the code itself.

## When to call `recall`
- At the start of a session, before making changes: recall relevant past
  decisions for the area you're about to touch.
- Before proposing an architectural change: recall if this was already
  decided/rejected before.

## When to call `list_memories`
- Once, at the very start of a new session, to load full project context.
